{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
  "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:14 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: JASTA permits any U.S. national injured by reason of an act of international terrorism to recover treble damages from a person who aids and abets by knowingly providing substantial assistance or who conspires with the person who committed such an act of international terrorism."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Waxman, it seems that you tie your analysis to knowledge of the Reina attacks rather than just general knowledge of terrorism."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You gave a variety of considerations to take into account in response to Justice Thomas's hypothetical, but it seems to me that given the facts, you ought to be able to give us a bottom line or not. Would that be covered by the statute or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I -- I guess I'm a little confused from your brief because it need -- from your brief, I thought you needed a direct connection between the assistance given and the actual act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- where the rubber meets the road here is in what is Step 3 of Halberstam, but, more significantly, the operative language of the statute, which means that even if -- of course, Twitter and -- and Meta and Google, YouTube knew from all these reports that, notwithstanding their efforts, there continued to be posted on their communication services messages, videos, whatever, that violated their"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you knew that ISIS was using your platform."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defendant (Waxman)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "where the culpable -- where the alleged culpable conduct is the failure to do more to prevent misuse of widely available services offered to the world at arm's length subject to enforced policies against terrorist content, it is not as a matter of law the knowing provision of substantial assistance to an act of international terrorism, absent specific knowledge of particular accounts or posts that were used to plan, commit, or proximately support the act of international terrorism that injured the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Just want to make sure I understand your position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. So I'm having a little bit of difficulty isolating exactly your argument, so let me -- let me put it to you this way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: I -- I -- I think you probably could, but when you say known terrorist, I -- I -- I'm not -- if it's just somebody who is affiliated with ISIS, you might have the connect -- the proximate connection, but --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Take Justice Kagan's hypothetical and substitute going back even further than the days of pagers to the days of -- of landline phones and phone booths."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Kneedler, a -- a few times, in talking about differences among hypothetical cases and real cases, you said this is really a societal judgment about who counts as complicit, who counts as culpable, and that seems right to me. But it seems to suggest that this should be a jury question, shouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. -- Mr. Kneedler, I'm -- I'm sorry to interrupt, but I -- I was hoping for an answer -- answer having something to do with the statutory text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I just want to make sure I understand how you think this is different from a material support statute, so if you have a communications business or a financial business or a food business or a travel business and you serve lots of customers, but you knowingly provide your services to a terrorist organization that you know is a terrorist organization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Again, because of the banking example, a bank may hold itself out to be open to all comers, but, in the --in the context of conducting that business, they may have an individualized encounter. Some -- you don't just open an account in most banks online or get a loan online. There's going to be some back and forth by which the bank will get to know something about the person it's doing business with or know that that person is affiliated --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 111,
        "start": 111
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What you may not have according to this is knowledge that with respect to the attacks that the person is now accusing you of assisting, you were helping those people who were involved in that act. Is that enough to get you out?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 124,
        "start": 124
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position, as I've said, that the assistance doesn't have to be connected to a specific act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0005-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 125,
        "start": 125
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The material support statute is both broader and narrower than aiding and abetting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 133,
        "start": 133
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- since you raised that point, you know, the statute, again, I --I do think focuses our attention on who aids and abets the person who committed such an act of international terrorism, but it doesn't -- it doesn't just focus us on the person, though that's helpful and it narrows things. It also says you must knowingly provide substantial assistance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Waxman and Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dd6c3d8c307d-0006-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Waxman and Mr. Kneedler and some of the amicus briefs, is that humanitarian and charitable organizations are going to be caught up in this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "dd6c3d8c307d304d7a04ee78c68af1c21a48a0a3e9724f757c9fd311bc316cdd",
